WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.442 --> 00:00:04.018
Unit twenty-one. Strong Passphrases!

2
00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:09.663
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:13.523
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.573 --> 00:00:17.823
Today we learn about Strong Passphrases. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:23.237
Password. Say it with me. Password!

6
00:00:26.744 --> 00:00:31.109
Passphrase. Say it with me. Passphrase!

7
00:00:34.586 --> 00:00:38.184
Long. Say it with me. Long!

8
00:00:41.722 --> 00:00:45.889
Words. Say it with me. Words!

9
00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:52.891
Guess. Say it with me. Guess!

10
00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.236
Secret. Say it with me. Secret!

11
00:01:03.718 --> 00:01:07.374
Unique. Say it with me. Unique!

12
00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:14.892
Account. Say it with me. Account!

13
00:01:18.384 --> 00:01:32.358
A passphrase is a password made of several random words, like 'purple tiger jumps rain'. Long passphrases are hard to guess but easy to remember. I keep a unique, secret one for each account.

14
00:01:32.407 --> 00:01:35.657
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:36.407 --> 00:01:42.066
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:42.116 --> 00:01:43.266
Long!

17
00:01:44.257 --> 00:01:49.760
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:50.960
Unique!

19
00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:58.824
Did you know? Each extra word in a passphrase makes it much harder for a computer to guess!

20
00:01:58.874 --> 00:02:01.280
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:02.059 --> 00:02:11.414
Think and answer. Why is a long passphrase stronger than a short password?

22
00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.629
Great answer!

23
00:02:13.596 --> 00:02:19.289
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:22.473
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

